{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$ is the *second derivative* of $y$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$, which is the derivative of $y$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$, we need to differentiate $y$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2e^{4x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=8e^{4x}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2e^{4x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{4x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\left(e^{4x}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[4x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2e^{4x}\\cdot4\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=8e^{4x}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[8e^{4x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=32e^{4x}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[8e^{4x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=8\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[e^{4x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=8\\left(e^{4x}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[4x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=8e^{4x}\\cdot4\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=32e^{4x}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=32e^{4x}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=2e^{4x}$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$32e^{4x}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac{e^{4x}}{8}$","correct":false},{"content":"$40e^{6x}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$8e^x$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
